# The TC39 proposal the corpus's `proposal:temporal@...` provenance names (corpus revision 24, milestone SJL-10.2).
#
# Every `proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#<clause-id>` entry is a clause of this proposal's specification text, the
# files below, at the revision both engines follow (Broiler.VM's JSD-0053, and Broiler.JS by JSD-0078's decision D1).
# The pinned ECMA-262 edition (ecma262.pin) does not contain Temporal, so the Temporal area cites this text instead.
# Its polyfill at the same revision, `polyfill/lib`, is the area's reference computation (`ref:temporalref@1`,
# decision D10), which scripts/conformance/generate_temporal_vectors.py holds to the git blob id of each of its 24
# files; where the text and the polyfill disagree, the text rules (decision D7) and the vector's provenance records
# the polyfill's answer as `overruled:temporalref@1=<outcome>`.
#
# The corpus archives none of these files and quotes no text of them. They were read from a blobless clone of the
# proposal taken on 2026-10-18 at SJL-10.1; each is named by its length and SHA-256, so a copy can be verified:
#
#   git -C <proposal-temporal> show e8cc03fc970a65a3359e8870e3b35e687ac94e55:spec/duration.html | sha256sum

